WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.346
Hi, I'm Creek!

00:00:02.346 --> 00:00:06.570
LeVJEPA learns video features with a single encoder and a single loss.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.034
Here's how it avoids the usual collapse.

00:00:10.433 --> 00:00:16.744
V-JEPA 2 avoids collapse with an averaged target network, a stop-gradient and a predictor.

00:00:16.744 --> 00:00:20.350
LeVJEPA drops all three for one regularizer, SIGReg.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.863
From each sixteen-frame clip, cut one global view and four local crops,

00:00:25.863 --> 00:00:28.088
all over the same stretch of time.

00:00:28.508 --> 00:00:32.080
Every view goes through the same encoder, in the same forward pass.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.760
The target is just the global view's own output.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.926
A small projector turns each clip token into an embedding, and the

00:00:38.926 --> 00:00:41.735
loss pulls every local embedding toward the global one.

00:00:42.155 --> 00:00:45.154
Alone, that collapses to one constant vector.

00:00:45.154 --> 00:00:51.152
SIGReg forbids it, pushing the batch toward an isotropic Gaussian, tested along random directions.

00:00:52.708 --> 00:00:56.891
A bidirectional encoder lets every frame see the whole clip, including frames

00:00:56.891 --> 00:00:58.285
that haven't happened yet.

00:00:58.705 --> 00:01:03.218
The shipped weights use block-causal attention: patches see their own frame and

00:01:03.218 --> 00:01:04.722
earlier ones, never later.

00:01:04.722 --> 00:01:06.226
It cost no accuracy.

00:01:06.646 --> 00:01:11.731
So a video's representation can grow as new frames arrive, without re-encoding the past.

00:01:11.731 --> 00:01:14.274
That's what streaming and world models need.

00:01:16.092 --> 00:01:20.313
The payoff: five point six to twenty point eight times less pretraining

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:24.183
compute than V-JEPA 2, trained for the same number of epochs.

00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:28.394
Collapse can be ruled out by the loss, not the architecture.

00:01:28.394 --> 00:01:30.817
And then the encoder is free to be causal.

00:01:34.025 --> 00:01:38.837
To recap: one encoder, one regularizer instead of three safeguards, and attention

00:01:38.837 --> 00:01:40.440
that only looks back.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.891
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:42.891 --> 00:01:43.471
I'm Creek.

00:01:43.471 --> 00:01:43.761
Bye!
